{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>to serve the service of the Tent of Meeting.</b> And further on, concerning the sons of Gershon, it says ״עֲבוֹדָה בְּאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״, because the service of the sons of Gershon is within the Tent of Meeting itself, for they carry the coverings of the mishkan and the Tent of Meeting its cover, etc. — unlike the sons of Merari, whose service is the planks and the sockets, etc., which constitute the service of the Tent of Meeting, for they carry the Tent of Meeting. Therefore it says <b>to serve</b> et … <b>the planks</b>, etc. — for these are the service of the Tent of Meeting. And therefore it did not bother to say merely ״לַצָּבָא״, since the verse has already specified its contents — unlike the service of the sons of Gershon, where it alerted you to the distinction between their service and the service of the sons of Kehat, because in both cases it says ״עֲבוֹדָה בָּאֹהֶל״ and there is no recognizable indication in its language of the difference between the two. For this reason it wrote a variation — ״לִצְבֹא צָבָא״, altered from what it wrote concerning the sons of Kehat, ״לַצָּבָא״. And on account of the distinction between the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, it alerted you through yet another variation, as we have written."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:06.837602792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}